SAP S/4HANA is the next-generation ERP system from SAP, built on the in-memory database HANA,
while SAP ECC is the older, traditional ERP system. S/4HANA offers advantages like real-time
data processing, improved performance, and a modern user interface with SAP Fiori,
whereas ECC relies on traditional databases and a more dated GUI.

SAP ECC (ERP Central Component):
-------------------------------
Database: Operates on various traditional relational databases like Oracle, SQL Server, or DB2.

Data Model: Has a more complex data model with multiple tables and potentially redundant data.

User Interface: Uses the traditional SAP GUI, which can be less user-friendly than S/4HANA's Fiori.

Processing: Often relies on batch processing and older integration methods like IDocs.

Scalability: On-premise deployment, with scalability potentially limited by infrastructure.

Cloud: Not available in the cloud, only on-premise.

SAP S/4HANA:
------------
Database:
Runs exclusively on the SAP HANA in-memory database, providing significantly faster data processing and analytics.

Data Model:
Features a simplified and optimized data model with fewer tables and less redundancy.

User Interface:
Offers a modern and intuitive user interface with SAP Fiori, enhancing user experience.

Processing:
Enables real-time data processing and analytics.

Scalability:
Supports both on-premise and cloud deployments, offering greater flexibility and scalability.

Integration:
Uses a modern API-first approach with REST APIs and OData services for better integration with other systems.